  "body": "## What is needed\n\nAdd a compact quick-op form to the Stock page. The form uses the commands of #3194.\n\n#3194 adds these parts:\n\n- `SketchRecipe` in `camcraft-geometry` (rectangle, circle, obround, regular polygon).\n- The undoable commands `CreateSketchRecipe`, `EditSketchRecipe` and `AddQuickOp` (`crates/app/src/commands/sketch_recipe.rs`).\n- The MCP tools `add_sketch_recipe`, `edit_sketch_recipe` and `add_quick_op`.\n\nThe PR of #3194 has no UI form. The form must give a user without a CAD model the same operation from the Stock page.\n\n## Design\n\n- A \"Quick op\" group on the Stock page, below the DXF profiles group.\n- A shape selector: rectangle, circle, obround, polygon.\n- The dimension fields of the selected shape. A polygon also has the side count and an across-flats or across-corners choice.\n- A tool selector (document tools), a depth field, and an \"Add quick op\" button. The button queues one `AddQuickOp`.\n- A recipe profile row on the Stock page shows its dimensions. An edit queues one `EditSketchRecipe`.\n- Show each refusal text of the command. Do not clamp a field.\n- Use plain machining terms. Do not copy vendor UI labels, parameter names or dialog flows.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A `CommandKind` variant for each command, with UI behaviour tests (labels, roles, enabled state, queued command).\n- The Stock page layout test is updated.\n- Before and after screenshots are in the PR body.\n\nFollow-up of #3194.\n",
